Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The measured failures show that the previous "one constrained token per step"
// policy still under-committed: it produced syntactically valid but extremely
// short SQL prefixes such as "SELECT <id>" and then ran out of steps before
// reaching a full query. Syntax is already perfect, so the problem is not
// grammar compliance; it is completion depth.
//
// This revision changes the in-span policy from token-by-token growth to
// symbol-level growth using ConstrainedSymbol with the full per-step token
// budget. That helper can spend multiple LM tokens to finish one parser symbol,
// which is much better matched to Spider SQL where important units like column
// names, table names, operators, and literals may require several tokens.
// The strategy is therefore:
//
// 1) Outside the constrained span, cheaply scan for "<<" with one
//    UnconstrainedChunk.
// 2) Inside the span, never do broad unconstrained sampling. Instead, repeatedly
//    ask ConstrainedSymbol to complete the next grammar symbol using the full
//    stepTokenBudget.
// 3) If the current SQL prefix is complete, immediately close with ">>".
// 4) If ConstrainedSymbol hits EOS or makes no progress, stop rather than
//    wandering.
// 5) If the parser detects a dead end, roll back to a valid constrained prefix;
//    if that repaired prefix is complete, close immediately, otherwise continue
//    symbol-level constrained generation.
//
// Compared with the previous attempt, the essential fix is replacing
// single-token constrained growth with larger symbol-level constrained growth.
// This directly targets the observed short-prefix failures while preserving the
// strong syntax guarantees and the required << >> wrapping.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: In the unconstrained-chunk branch we are either still
//   outside the span or we just opened it with currentConstrainedOut := [],
//   which is valid by precondition. In the symbol-growth branch,
//   ConstrainedSymbol returns a new constrained prefix currentSym that is used
//   directly as currentConstrainedOut, so validity is preserved. In the close
//   branch insideConstrainedOut becomes false, making the implication vacuous.
//   In the rollback branch, RollbackConstrainedSpan restores a valid prefix;
//   any subsequent close again makes the implication vacuous, and otherwise we
//   continue from that repaired valid prefix.
// suffix: Outside the span the invariant is vacuous; opening on "<<" sets an
//   empty constrained suffix, so it holds trivially. In the symbol-growth
//   branch we rebuild generated as stablePrefix + currentSym, so the suffix of
//   length |currentSym| is exactly currentSym. Closing makes the implication
//   vacuous. Rollback explicitly restores generated/currentConstrainedOut to a
//   matching constrained suffix before either closing or continuing.
// progress: UnconstrainedChunk appends stepsUsed tokens and we add exactly
//   stepsUsed to steps. Each ConstrainedSymbol branch appends
//   |currentSym| - |oldCurrent| tokens to generated and increments steps by the
//   returned stepsUsed; since one LM step can add at most one token,
//   |currentSym| - |oldCurrent| <= stepsUsed, so
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps is preserved. Each close appends
//   exactly one token and increments steps by 1. Rollback may shrink generated,
//   which only helps the bound.
// cost accounting: We return cost := steps. UnconstrainedChunk contributes its
//   returned stepsUsed, ConstrainedSymbol contributes its returned stepsUsed,
//   and each CloseConstrainedSpan contributes 1. Pure queries and rollback do
//   not affect steps. The guard steps < maxSteps and checks on remaining budget
//   ensure steps never exceeds maxSteps, so cost <= maxSteps.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

var steps: nat := 0;

while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> generated[|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|..] == currentConstrainedOut
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
  decreases maxSteps - steps
{
  if !insideConstrainedOut {
    var chunkBudget: nat := maxSteps - steps;
    var chunkedGenerated, stoppedOnOpenSpan, stoppedOnEos, stepsUsed := helpers.UnconstrainedChunk(
      lm, prompt, generated, chunkBudget, "<<", eosToken
